From: TactiQ OS <andrey@tactiq.ai>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] init: daemons never use ttys (drop the true branch of
 init_daemons_use_tty)

The tunable init_daemons_use_tty grants every domain with the daemon
attribute read and write on all ttys, tty_device_t included, when it is
switched on. It is off by default, but in the built policy it is a
boolean (booleanif in the CIL), so a process allowed to set booleans can
switch it on at run time. Every TactiQ AI agent domain is started by
init_daemon_domain() and so carries the daemon attribute: with the
boolean on, an agent could open /dev/ttyS*, /dev/ttyUSB* or
/dev/ttyACM* and speak Modbus RTU to a PLC past agentgateway and
tactiq-stop.

tactiq_fixes 2.7.0 asserts that an AI agent opens no serial device
(assertion 11). With this block in place that assertion fails the build
on the true branch alone (dev-build-rc11, 18.11.2026, no other
violation reported). This patch keeps the false branch, which is the
default behaviour, unconditionally, and removes the true branch. The
tunable declaration is left in place so nothing that names it breaks;
switching it no longer changes the policy.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [TactiQ OS specific hardening]

Signed-off-by: TactiQ OS <andrey@tactiq.ai>
---
 policy/modules/system/init.te | 17 ++++++-----------
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 11 deletions(-)

diff --git a/policy/modules/system/init.te b/policy/modules/system/init.te
index 8188f8a..427fcd3 100644
--- a/policy/modules/system/init.te
+++ b/policy/modules/system/init.te
@@ -1665,17 +1665,12 @@ ifdef(`init_systemd',`
 	')
 ')
 
-tunable_policy(`init_daemons_use_tty',`
-	term_use_unallocated_ttys(daemon)
-	term_use_generic_ptys(daemon)
-	term_use_all_ttys(daemon)
-	term_use_all_ptys(daemon)
-',`
-	term_dontaudit_use_unallocated_ttys(daemon)
-	term_dontaudit_use_generic_ptys(daemon)
-	term_dontaudit_use_all_ttys(daemon)
-	term_dontaudit_use_all_ptys(daemon)
- ')
+# TactiQ OS: the tunable's true branch is removed, its false branch is
+# kept unconditionally. See 0006-init-daemons-never-use-ttys.patch.
+term_dontaudit_use_unallocated_ttys(daemon)
+term_dontaudit_use_generic_ptys(daemon)
+term_dontaudit_use_all_ttys(daemon)
+term_dontaudit_use_all_ptys(daemon)
 
 tunable_policy(`use_nfs_home_dirs',`
 	fs_dontaudit_rw_nfs_files(daemon)
